# Stremio `/meta` ResourceResponse

If the catalog lists titles but clicking one shows "No metadata was found!",
the `/meta` JSON shape is wrong. Do not "fix" this by dropping the wrapper
or wrapping `meta` in an array.

Required shapes:

- `/catalog/...` → `{ "metas": [ MetaPreview, ... ] }`
- `/meta/...` → `{ "meta": { ...Meta Object } }`  (object, NEVER an array, NEVER a bare object)
- `/stream/...` → `{ "streams": [ Stream, ... ] }`

The addon SDK `protocol.md` example that shows `"meta": [ {...} ]` is wrong.
Cinemeta (`/meta/movie/tt1254207.json`) and `stremio-core`'s `ResourceResponse::Meta`
are the spec: `{ "meta": { "id", "type", ... } }`.

For movies, set `behaviorHints.defaultVideoId` to the meta id so Stremio Web
opens streams instead of Season 0 / Episode 1.

`released` must be RFC3339 (`2026-05-06T00:00:00.000Z`). A date-only string
makes stremio-core reject the whole Meta object — same empty detail page,
even with the correct `{ "meta": ... }` wrapper.

Helpers already in the repo: `as_meta_resource()` in `addon/build_addon.py` and
`normalizeMetaBody()` in `debrid-app/lib/addon-data.js`. Keep both. Prove with
`python3 tests/test_meta_protocol.py` and a curl of `/meta/movie/<id>.json`
that top-level keys are `["meta"]` and `meta` is a dict.

Do not point `poster` at `tu.djhdhs.us` or `*.vercel.app` for clients. Forum
covers Cloudflare-challenge requests without `Referer: https://sehuatang.org/`,
and Vercel-proxied images force the debrid site to stay online. Use public DMM
covers: catalog `poster` is `{code}ps.jpg`, detail `background` is `{code}pl.jpg`
(`dmm_poster()` / `withPublicPosters()`). Never use fanart as the catalog poster.

`/stream` with Torbox must `POST /createtorrent` (multipart magnet), keep the
`torrent_id` (including `DUPLICATE_ITEM` / `mylist` by hash), and return
`/play?service=torbox&token=&torrent_id=&file_id=`. `/play` calls `requestdl`
without redirect/zip and 302s to the CDN file URL. Never give Stremio
`requestdl?redirect=true` or `zip_link=true`.

Stream rows follow Torrentio layout: `name` is the left badge (`Torbox\n5.19G`),
`description` is the right detail. Torrent fallback is `{ infoHash }`, never
`{ url: "magnet:..." }`. Stremio Web cannot play magnets.
